    {
      "_comment": [
        "Credential and scheduling calls. Appendix B does not exclude these, so",
        "they belong in the profile; they were simply missing from the first",
        "draft. They are also what runc's init needs before execve, which is how",
        "the omission surfaced: Docker installs the filter before container",
        "setup finishes, whereas Zygo's launcher installs it as the last step",
        "before execve."
      ],
      "names": [
        "setfsgid",
        "setfsuid",
        "setgid",
        "setgroups",
        "setpriority",
        "setregid",
        "setresgid",
        "setresuid",
        "setreuid",
        "setrlimit",
        "setuid",
        "sched_rr_get_interval",
        "sched_setaffinity",
        "sched_setattr",
        "sched_getattr",
        "sched_setparam",
        "sched_setscheduler"
      ],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW"
    },
    {
      "_comment": "fork() and thread creation. CLONE_NEWUSER and friends are not reachable here because the flags below exclude every CLONE_NEW* bit.",
      "names": ["clone"],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW",
      "args": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "value": 2114060288,
          "valueTwo": 0,
          "op": "SCMP_CMP_MASKED_EQ"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "names": ["clone3"],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
      "errnoRet": 38,
      "_comment": "ENOSYS makes glibc fall back to clone(), where the flag filter above applies."
    },
    {
      "_comment": "personality(0) and the Linux-native variants only; ADDR_NO_RANDOMIZE and friends stay blocked.",
      "names": ["personality"],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW",
      "args": [{ "index": 0, "value": 0, "op": "SCMP_CMP_EQ" }]
    },
    {
      "names": ["personality"],
      "action": "SCMP_ACT_ALLOW",
